  "procedures": [],
  "course": {
    "narrative": "A 68-year-old male with multiple comorbidities including stage III CKD presented for evaluation of acute on chronic kidney failure after blood work showed a creatinine elevation to 2.3. He reported taking 12 to 13 pills of Chinese herbs and dietary supplements for a year until stopping 2-3 weeks prior. He also described morning dizziness and home blood pressures under 100/60. Physical exam revealed orthostatic dizziness. Labs showed an elevated creatinine of 2.3 and CK of 653. The clinician recommended avoiding NSAIDs and Chinese herbs, decreasing dosages of atenolol, enalapril, and Lasix, stopping Crestor, checking a renal ultrasound, obtaining repeat labs, and following up in two weeks.",
